WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:02.420
- Here are the nominees for
achievement in directing.

00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:04.610
- We're just a few very busy months away

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:05.700
from the Academy Awards

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:06.820
so it's probably a good time

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:08.730
to start making some
early Oscar predictions,

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:09.563
am I right?

00:00:09.563 --> 00:00:11.240
This is what we do with our free time.

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:12.640
We're gonna tell you which directors

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:15.170
we think may snag an
Oscar nomination right now

00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:16.130
on the Ketchup.

00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:18.330
There are some huge
names on our early list,

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:19.730
starting with Quentin Tarantino

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:21.130
and his ninth studio film,

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:22.650
Once Upon a Time in Hollywood,

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:25.830
which is certified fresh
at 85% on the tomato meter.

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:27.500
After a somewhat mediocre response

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:30.100
to his last effort in
2015's The Hateful Eight,

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:31.380
Tarantino enlisted the help

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:33.710
of some guys named Leo
and Brad this time around

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:35.040
and they gave two of the most

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:37.450
universally acclaimed
performances of the year.

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:40.020
Still can't believe this was
their first film together.

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:42.130
- It's official, old buddy.

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:43.020
I'm a has-been.

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:45.450
- Tarantino will live to get
his third Oscar nomination

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:47.300
and first win in the directing category,

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:50.430
having previously been nominated
for 1994's Pulp Fiction

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:52.540
and 2009's Inglorious Bastards,

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:54.220
both certified fresh, by the way.

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:56.260
- I'm the one who buys
it, I know how good it is.

00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:57.500
- Someone else who knows

00:00:57.500 --> 00:00:59.040
a little bit about being nominated

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:01.080
is the iconic Martin Scorsese.

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:02.960
The 76-year-old director is back

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:04.360
with Netflix's The Irishman

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:05.920
and yes, there's a theme here.

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:07.800
This film is loaded with huge names,

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:08.950
like Robert De Niro,

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:11.420
Al Pacino, Joe Pesci, and Harvey Keitel.

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:13.790
- Hiya Frank, this is Jimmy Hoffa.

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:15.290
- After five nominations,

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:17.260
2006 certified fresh The Departed

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:20.470
gave Marty his first
directing win after 25 years.

00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:21.670
So I guess the pressure's off,

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:23.100
but with a little help from his friends

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:24.330
Bob, Al, and Joe,

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:26.910
not to mention new state-of-the-art
de-aging technology,

00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:29.380
it's like Scorsese's just getting started.

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:30.250
- Where are you going?

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:31.083
- I'm going to work.

00:01:31.083 --> 00:01:33.450
- Greta Gerwig has also made this list

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:35.630
for her upcoming
adaptation of Little Women,

00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:37.370
starring Timothee Chalamet,

00:01:37.370 --> 00:01:39.870
Saoirse Ronan, Emma
Watson, and Meryl Streep.

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:41.150
I mean the casting crew combined

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:43.600
is nearly 35 Oscar nominations.

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:44.890
- You are not married--
- Well,

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:46.170
that's because I'm rich.

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:48.590
- And Greta is coming off
a directing nomination

00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:50.920
from 2018's Oscars for Lady Bird.

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:53.010
This time Gerwig is
adapting a popular story

00:01:53.010 --> 00:01:54.980
that has done well at
the Oscars in the past,

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:57.960
including a best picture
win for 1949's version

00:01:57.960 --> 00:01:59.860
of Little Women, with Elizabeth Taylor,

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:02.140
so the odds of being nominated
could be in her favor.

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:03.930
Next up is James Mangold

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:06.620
from the true life tale, Ford V Ferrari.

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:09.160
Currently fresh at 89%
on the tomato meter.

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:11.840
Much like Taratino, Mangold
had a couple of megstars

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:15.020
of his own to work with: Matt
Damon and Christian Bale.

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:16.160
- Looks aren't everything.

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:17.730
- But when it comes to the Oscars,

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:20.190
Mangold has directed
both Reese Witherspoon

00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:22.920
to a best actress win
for 2005's Walk the Line,

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:25.590
and Angelina Jolie to a
best supporting actress win

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:27.730
for 1999's Girl Interrupted,

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:29.080
but his only nomination

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:30.840
came in the adapted screenplay category

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:32.400
for 2017's Logan.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:33.860
So now seems like the perfect time

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:35.800
for him to join the best director race.

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:37.594
Let's just hope he's a Ford in this case.

00:02:37.594 --> 00:02:38.960
(laughing)

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:41.170
And finally rounding out the fifth spot

00:02:41.170 --> 00:02:42.260
in our early predictions

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:44.620
is South Korean director Bong Joon Ho,

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:47.790
whose film Parasite is
a certified fresh 100%

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:48.940
on the tomato meter.

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:50.260
The social political satire

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:52.480
which explores the evils
of wealth, inequality,

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:54.670
and class discrimination
earned the top prize

00:02:54.670 --> 00:02:55.940
at the Cannes film festival.

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:58.470
And while he may not have
a who's who of a cast

00:02:58.470 --> 00:03:00.450
like the other directors
that we just mentioned,

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:02.310
the Rotten Tomatoes critics consensus

00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:03.830
is that Parasite shows a director

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:06.260
quote in near total command of his craft.

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:09.270
And since Alfonso Cuaron just
became the first director

00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:10.280
of a foreign language film

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:13.210
to win the best director
Oscar for last year's Roma,

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:15.117
why not Bong Joon Ho this year?

00:03:15.117 --> 00:03:17.140
(speaking in foreign language)

00:03:17.140 --> 00:03:18.840
So I wanna kick it over to you guys now.

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:19.860
Which of these directors

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:21.300
do you think has the best chance

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:22.420
to take home the Oscar?

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:23.960
Are there any names that we left off

00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:25.390
that you feel are more deserving?

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:27.550
And can the director of
a foreign language film

00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:29.010
win two years in a row?

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:30.480
Let us know all your thoughts and feelings

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:31.320
in the comments section,

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:32.670
and for more movie news,

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:34.560
head on over to rottentomatoes.com.

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:36.280
As always, thanks for
watching The Ketchup.

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:38.630
I'm Naz Perez, and I'll
see you guys next time.

